 34S  c  Multi-nucleon transfer and deep-inelastic binary grazing reactions.    
 34S  c  2010WaZT: a 215-MeV {+36}S{+9+} beam was produced from the XTU-Tandem  
 34S 2c  ALPI-superconducting linear accelerator complex at the INFN Legnaro    
 34S 3c  National Laboratory, Italy. The target was 300-|mg/cm{+2}, 99.7%       
 34S 4c  enriched {+208}Pb on a 20-|mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. Projectile-like   
 34S 5c  fragments produced in binary grazing reactions were separated and      
 34S 6c  identified by the PRISMA spectrometer. |g rays were detected using the 
 34S 7c  CLARA array of 22 escape-suppressed Ge clover detectors covering the   
 34S 8c  azimuthal angles from 98|' to 180|'. Measured E|g with Doppler         
 34S 9c  corrections, I|g, and ({+34}S)|g-coin. Deduced levels. Compared with  
 34S Ac  shell-model calculations. Also see 2010Wa12 and 2010Wa20 from the same 
 34S Bc  experiments.                                                           
 34S  cG E,RI$From Table 6.11 of 2010WaZT.                                       
 34S  cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies in 2010WaZT.             
 34S  cL J$As given in 2010WaZT, based on shell-model calculations.             
